   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">void ThrowAsException (const <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"cl_ara_core_ErrorCode_538b08.html\">ara::core::ErrorCode</a> &amp;errorCode) const noexcept(false) override;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>Creates a new instance of <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"cl_ara_com_ComException_85bfb4.html\">ara::com::ComException</a> from errorCode and throws it. As per <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CORE_10304\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf)\">[SWS_CORE_10304]</a>, this function does not participate in overload resolution when C++ exceptions are disabled in the compiler toolchain.</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
